1
00:00:07,168 --> 00:00:12,869
-==www.RagBear.com==- 是, 首相  第1季第1集

2
00:00:12,869 --> 00:00:21,289
<font color="#4096d1">本字幕仅供学习交流，严禁用于商业用途

3
00:00:22,165 --> 00:00:31,407
<font color="#4096d1">-=破烂熊字幕组=- 翻译:Celeste 校对&时间轴:tpring

4
00:00:36,072 --> 00:00:38,660
大展宏图

5
00:00:47,356 --> 00:00:49,179
(国防部)
(Ministry of Defence)

6
00:01:14,835 --> 00:01:16,303
告诉我 将军 热线在哪里?
Tell me, General. Where's the hotline?

7
00:01:17,475 --> 00:01:18,943
哪一条?      连接俄国的那一条
Which one? The one to Russia.

8
00:01:20,115 --> 00:01:22,185
"红色热线" 先生
The red hotline, sir.

9
00:01:22,355 --> 00:01:24,505
在唐宁街
It's in Downing Street.

10
00:01:24,675 --> 00:01:27,389
紧急情况下我能直接接通苏联主席吗?
I can get through to the Soviet president?

11
00:01:27,389 --> 00:01:28,443
理论上可以
Theoretically, yes.

12
00:01:28,443 --> 00:01:31,147
理论上?     我们是这么跟记者说的
Theoretically? That's what we tell journalists.

13
00:01:31,315 --> 00:01:35,706
确实接通过一次克林姆林宫 那边是个接线员
We once get through to a switchboard operator.

14
00:01:35,875 --> 00:01:40,665
他不能转过去吗?     不知道 他英语不好
Couldn't he put you through? Never found out.

15
00:01:40,835 --> 00:01:43,303
这条线多久测试一次?     尽量少测试
How often is it tested? Not too often.

16
00:01:43,475 --> 00:01:45,989
否则会给另一端带来不必要的恐慌
It creates unnecessary panic at the other end,

17
00:01:46,155 --> 00:01:50,626
考虑到核武器 还是避免恐慌为好
avoid panic where nuclear weapons are concerned.

18
00:01:50,795 --> 00:01:53,548
对哦     就是这个
Yes. Now, this is it.

19
00:01:53,755 --> 00:01:55,746
啊 好
Ah, good.

20
00:01:56,995 --> 00:02:00,510
这是什么?     扳机 首相
What is it? The trigger, Prime Minister.

21
00:02:00,675 --> 00:02:03,189
扳机?     核武器扳机 按钮
The trigger? The nuclear trigger, the button.

22
00:02:03,355 --> 00:02:05,789
这个?     间接地说 是的
This? Indirectly, yes.

23
00:02:06,395 --> 00:02:09,705
这条电报线直通诺伍德海军基地
This is the telex communication with HMS Northwood.

24
00:02:09,875 --> 00:02:15,313
您发一个电码 基地通讯员回一个确认码
You send a coded signal and Northwood sends another signal.

25
00:02:15,515 --> 00:02:17,506
这样他就知道是您了
So he knows it's from you.

26
00:02:17,715 --> 00:02:20,229
一旦您的指令被确认
When the instruction's been authenticated,

27
00:02:20,395 --> 00:02:24,388
基地会下令给一艘北极星潜艇 他们就按按钮
Northwood sends a command to a Polaris submarine.

28
00:02:24,595 --> 00:02:26,984
就这样?     就这样
Just like that? Just like that.

29
00:02:27,155 --> 00:02:29,669
只要我下命令?     只要您下命令
When I say so? When you say so.

30
00:02:30,315 --> 00:02:32,704
不会有人跟我争论吗?
Wouldn't anybody argue with me?

31
00:02:33,595 --> 00:02:36,314
军人的天职是服从 不是提问
Serving officers obey orders without question.

32
00:02:36,475 --> 00:02:38,830
如果我那时喝醉了呢?
What if I were to get drunk?

33
00:02:38,995 --> 00:02:42,192
基本上 您别喝醉比较安全
On the whole, it would be safer if you didn't.

34
00:02:42,355 --> 00:02:43,754
天哪
Blimey!

35
00:02:43,915 --> 00:02:46,907
这是您的工作 是您要干的 首相
It's your job and you wanted it, Prime Minister.

36
00:02:47,075 --> 00:02:50,863
假设我昏了头呢?     内阁会发现的
Supposing I were to go off my rocker? The Cabinet might notice.

37
00:02:51,035 --> 00:02:55,825
我可不指望 说真的 要是我下完令反悔了呢?
I wouldn't count on it. supposing I did and then changed my mind?

38
00:02:56,035 --> 00:02:59,152
没关系 反正也没人会发现了 不是吗?
That's all right. No one would ever know, would they?

39
00:03:01,635 --> 00:03:03,122
我们有多少核弹头?
How many bombs are there?

40
00:03:03,122 --> 00:03:07,045
4艘北极星核潜艇 每艘16颗 各3个弹头
Four Polaris submarines, 16 missiles on each.

41
00:03:07,045 --> 00:03:09,707
总共呢?      192
But how many actual bombs? 192.

42
00:03:09,915 --> 00:03:13,749
每一颗至少比广岛的强大5倍
Each one at least five times the power of the Hiroshima bomb.

43
00:03:13,955 --> 00:03:16,310
我知道您怎么想 "不太多"?
You're thinking, ''Not very many.''

44
00:03:16,515 --> 00:03:19,313
我不知道 似乎足够了
I don't know. That seems enough.

45
00:03:19,515 --> 00:03:23,269
比起1200颗瞄准英国的苏联核弹 不算多
Not with 1200 Soviet missiles trained on Britain

46
00:03:23,475 --> 00:03:25,670
1200?      嗯
1200? Hmm.

47
00:03:25,835 --> 00:03:29,104
反正大不列颠总是以寡击众
Britain's always fought against the odds

48
00:03:29,104 --> 00:03:30,546
西班牙无敌舰队 不列颠之战
the Armada, Battle of Britain.

49
00:03:30,546 --> 00:03:34,632
是的 等我们拥有三叉戟 我们的火力会大大增强
Yes, and we'll have more firepower when we get Trident.

50
00:03:34,795 --> 00:03:37,263
眼下 谢天谢地还有陆军
Thank goodness for conventional forces!

51
00:03:37,435 --> 00:03:40,711
陆军最多能拖住俄国人72小时
They would hold the Russians for at most 72 hours.

52
00:03:40,915 --> 00:03:42,906
就这?      嗯
Is that all? Hmm.

53
00:03:43,075 --> 00:03:44,420
所以如果有紧急情况发生
So in an emergency

54
00:03:44,420 --> 00:03:46,830
我就得当机立断作出决定?
I would have to make an instant decision?

55
00:03:46,830 --> 00:03:49,747
不 您至少有12小时      12小时?
No, you'd probably have 12 hours. 12 hours?

56
00:03:49,915 --> 00:03:52,270
我们不应该改善这个情况吗?
Shouldn't we do something about this?

57
00:03:52,475 --> 00:03:56,991
是 但20年以来 政客们总说他们养不起陆军
politicians have said they can't afford the conventional forces.

58
00:03:57,195 --> 00:04:00,187
陆军太贵了 首相
Conventional forces are very expensive, Prime Minister.

59
00:04:00,355 --> 00:04:02,823
按一下按钮便宜很多很多
Much cheaper just to press a button.

60
00:04:05,075 --> 00:04:07,589
那么这次会议您觉得多长时间为好?
So how long should we allow for this meeting?

61
00:04:07,755 --> 00:04:09,825
72小时...      好的
72 hours... Fine.

62
00:04:11,915 --> 00:04:14,429
只是新西兰专员而已
It's only the New Zealand High Commissioner.

63
00:04:15,915 --> 00:04:18,270
72小时是不是太慷慨了点?
Isn't 72 hours a bit generous?

64
00:04:19,195 --> 00:04:22,585
我只是在想我们能抵挡俄国人多长时间
I was just thinking how long we could hold the Russians.

65
00:04:22,755 --> 00:04:26,748
如果我们能说服美国人加强他们的陆军...
If we persuaded the Americans to strengthen THEIR forces...

66
00:04:26,955 --> 00:04:29,423
我觉得这样不会有什么改变
I don't think it'll make much difference.

67
00:04:29,595 --> 00:04:32,792
在德国的美国军队都磕药
The American troops in Germany are all so drug-ridden,

68
00:04:32,955 --> 00:04:35,469
他们也不知道自己是哪一边的
they don't know which side they're on anyway.

69
00:04:35,635 --> 00:04:38,069
上次北约演习的时候
And during the last NATO exercises,

70
00:04:38,235 --> 00:04:40,129
美国大兵在树林里解散
the U.S. troops dispersed

71
00:04:40,129 --> 00:04:42,322
然后和女性士兵一起去了树林里野餐
and picnicked in the woods with lady soldiers.

72
00:04:44,235 --> 00:04:45,895
那么其他的北约军队呢?
What about the other NATO armies?

73
00:04:45,895 --> 00:04:48,570
他们很好 至少在工作日的时候
They're all right. On weekdays, anyway.

74
00:04:49,315 --> 00:04:50,828
工作日?
Weekdays?

75
00:04:50,995 --> 00:04:54,510
对 荷兰 丹麦 比利时军队周末要回家的
The Dutch, Danish and Belgian armies go home for the weekend.

76
00:04:54,675 --> 00:04:56,919
所以 假定俄国人真要侵略
So if the Russians are to invade

77
00:04:56,919 --> 00:04:58,838
我们希望他们在周一至周五间侵略?
we'd prefer them to do it between Mondays and Fridays?

78
00:04:59,995 --> 00:05:02,066
很多人知道这件事吗?
Is this widely known?

79
00:05:02,066 --> 00:05:04,265
既然我都知道了 俄国人肯定知道
If I know it, I'm sure the Russians do.

80
00:05:04,265 --> 00:05:06,528
克林姆林宫得到北约消息的速度
The Kremlin usually gets NATO information

81
00:05:06,528 --> 00:05:08,614
通常比我们唐宁街10号快
before it filters through to Number 10.

82
00:05:10,355 --> 00:05:13,586
所以我们得依赖三叉戟?      等它送来
So it comes back to Trident? When it comes.

83
00:05:13,755 --> 00:05:16,223
如果它能用      如果它能...
If it works. If it wor...

84
00:05:17,875 --> 00:05:21,913
你说什么?      通常新来的武器
What do you mean? Normally, when new weapons are delivered,

85
00:05:21,913 --> 00:05:24,002
弹头都无法配合火箭架
the warheads don't fit the ends of the rockets.

86
00:05:25,675 --> 00:05:28,295
北极星就是这样 您知道的
That's what happened to Polaris. You know the sort of thing

87
00:05:28,295 --> 00:05:30,880
电线不行啦 芯片出错啦
wiring faults, microchip failure.

88
00:05:30,880 --> 00:05:34,013
有好几年我们都无法正常发射北极星
We couldn't fire Polaris for some years.

89
00:05:34,013 --> 00:05:37,042
巡航导弹可能也是 还有三叉戟
Cruise is probably the same. Trident might be too.

90
00:05:37,077 --> 00:05:39,189
这简直不能容忍 我们该把制造商送上法庭
We should take the manufacturers to court.

91
00:05:39,395 --> 00:05:41,575
我们不能冒被媒体发现的险
We can't risk the publicity

92
00:05:41,575 --> 00:05:42,455
国家安全 他们是知道的
security and they know it!

93
00:05:43,035 --> 00:05:44,843
那就不能换一个制造商?
We should change the manufacturers.

94
00:05:44,843 --> 00:05:45,967
我们总在换的
We do all the time.

95
00:05:46,995 --> 00:05:49,526
制造商也明白 这就是为什么
The manufacturers know that too. That's why

96
00:05:49,526 --> 00:05:51,497
一枚鱼雷击中了高尔夫球场
that torpedo landed on Sandwich golf course.

97
00:05:53,555 --> 00:05:57,150
高尔夫球场?我没在报纸上看到
Sandwich golf course? I didn't read that in the papers.

98
00:05:57,355 --> 00:05:59,823
当然不会 政府掩盖了消息
Of course not. There was a cover-up.

99
00:05:59,995 --> 00:06:01,408
只是第二天早上球员们
The members just found a new bunker

100
00:06:01,408 --> 00:06:03,483
发现第七道旁边多了条沟
on the 7th fairway the next morning.

101
00:06:05,435 --> 00:06:07,619
所以鱼雷都不能正常工作?
So the torpedoes don't work either?

102
00:06:07,619 --> 00:06:10,964
不 只是新的 其他的都可以
No, only the new ones. The others are fine.

103
00:06:11,115 --> 00:06:14,152
二战时候设计出来的的那些
The ones designed during the Second World War.

104
00:06:14,355 --> 00:06:17,347
40年前的?      对 它们久经测试
Over 40 years ago? They had lots of testing.

105
00:06:17,515 --> 00:06:20,712
现代武器很难做完这些测试      为什么?
You can't afford that with the modern ones. Why not?

106
00:06:20,875 --> 00:06:24,638
如果爆发核战 首相 时间不会久到
Well, if there's a nuclear war, it won't last long enough

107
00:06:24,638 --> 00:06:26,283
能让武器测试完为止
for the weapons to be tested.

108
00:06:26,318 --> 00:06:29,710
关于国防还有什么事情我得知道的?
Are there other things I don't know about the UK's defence?

109
00:06:29,915 --> 00:06:34,352
我不知道 首相 我不知道你不知道什么
I don't know, Prime Minister. I don't know what you don't know.

110
00:06:34,555 --> 00:06:36,341
不过如果您需要不同意见 我知道
The government's chief scientific adviser

111
00:06:36,341 --> 00:06:40,296
政府首席科学顾问和国防部的看法不太一样
sees the problem differently from the MoD.

112
00:06:40,296 --> 00:06:41,914
我现在就想见他
I'd like to see him now.

113
00:06:41,914 --> 00:06:43,687
晚一点邀请他来喝杯酒比较明智
A late drink might be wiser.

114
00:06:43,687 --> 00:06:46,063
最好别让内阁办公室知道
Better not to let the Cabinet Office know.

115
00:06:46,235 --> 00:06:47,342
汉弗莱爵士会不高兴的
Sir Humphrey gets upset.

116
00:06:47,342 --> 00:06:50,115
他不认为那位顾问属于我们的人
He doesn't regard him as one of us.

117
00:06:50,115 --> 00:06:52,514
我记得他在阿荷姆得过优秀军人勋章
I thought he won the DSO at Arnhem.

118
00:06:52,675 --> 00:06:56,145
这也不能弥补他古怪的奥地利口音
That doesn't make up for speaking with an Austrian accent.

119
00:06:56,315 --> 00:07:00,194
他没进过牛津剑桥 甚至伦敦政经学院
He didn't go to Oxford or Cambridge even go to the LSE.

120
00:07:03,595 --> 00:07:06,632
首相 您相信核武防御吗?
Prime Minister, you believe in the nuclear deterrent?

121
00:07:06,835 --> 00:07:08,826
哦 是的      为什么?
Oh, yes. Why?

122
00:07:08,995 --> 00:07:10,906
什么?      为什么?
Pardon? Why?

123
00:07:11,115 --> 00:07:13,231
因为它能防御
Because it deters.

124
00:07:14,115 --> 00:07:16,106
谁?      什么?
Whom? Pardon?

125
00:07:16,275 --> 00:07:20,587
谁?它防御谁?      防御俄国入侵
Whom? Whom does it deter? The Russians from attacking us.

126
00:07:20,795 --> 00:07:22,308
为什么?      什么?
Why? Pardon?

127
00:07:22,475 --> 00:07:23,794
什么?
Why?

128
00:07:23,955 --> 00:07:27,186
他们知道 如果他们侵略我就按按钮
They know if they launched an attack, I'd press the button.

129
00:07:27,395 --> 00:07:29,863
你会吗?      为什么不会?
You would? Well, wouldn't I?

130
00:07:30,035 --> 00:07:32,026
你会吗?
Well, would you?

131
00:07:32,195 --> 00:07:34,709
最后关头 我当然会
At the last resort, yes, I certainly would.

132
00:07:34,875 --> 00:07:37,514
我想我当然会的 当然
Well, I think I certainly would. Yes.

133
00:07:38,675 --> 00:07:40,946
几时才算最后关头呢?
And what is the last resort?

134
00:07:41,927 --> 00:07:43,470
如果俄国侵略西欧的话
If the Russians invaded western Europe.

135
00:07:43,470 --> 00:07:45,591
可你只有12小时 所以
You only have 12 hours to decide, so you're saying

136
00:07:45,591 --> 00:07:47,507
你的最后关头就是最初反应?
the last resort is the first response?

137
00:07:48,435 --> 00:07:50,312
是吗?
Am I?

138
00:07:50,515 --> 00:07:55,384
不用担心 俄国怎么会想要整个欧洲?
Why should the Russians annex the whole of Europe?

139
00:07:55,555 --> 00:07:58,023
他们连阿富汗都控制不了
They can't even control Afghanistan.

140
00:07:58,635 --> 00:08:02,150
不 如果他们尝试侵略 会用"香肠战术"
No, if they try anything, it will be salami tactics.

141
00:08:02,355 --> 00:08:04,823
香肠?      一片接一片
Salami tactics? Slice by slice.

142
00:08:05,675 --> 00:08:08,064
每次一小片儿
One small piece at a time.

143
00:08:08,235 --> 00:08:11,591
当他们侵略西柏林的时候你会按下按钮吗?
So will you press the button if they invade West Berlin?

144
00:08:12,355 --> 00:08:15,153
看情况      什么情况?
It all depends. On what?

145
00:08:15,355 --> 00:08:17,346
好吧 第一步
Scenario one.

146
00:08:17,955 --> 00:08:20,423
西柏林暴动
Riots in West Berlin,

147
00:08:20,595 --> 00:08:22,790
建筑物在燃烧
buildings in flames.

148
00:08:22,955 --> 00:08:28,188
东柏林消防队跨界前来救援 你按吗?
East German fire brigade crosses the border. Would you press?

149
00:08:28,875 --> 00:08:32,788
东柏林警察也过来了 按吗?
The East German police come with them. The button...?

150
00:08:32,995 --> 00:08:36,988
然后是军队 更多的军队 他们说是来控制骚乱的
Then some troops, more troops just for riot control, they say.

151
00:08:37,475 --> 00:08:42,230
再然后 俄国军队代替了东德 按吗?
East German troops are replaced by Russian troops. Button?

152
00:08:43,035 --> 00:08:45,503
俄国军队不肯走了
Then the Russian troops don't go.

153
00:08:45,675 --> 00:08:49,463
他们受邀留下援助民政部门
They are invited to stay to support civilian administration.

154
00:08:49,635 --> 00:08:53,628
民政部门关闭了道路和机场
The civilian administration closes roads and Tempelhof Airport.

155
00:08:54,275 --> 00:08:57,745
现在要按吗?       我需要时间考虑
Now you press the button? I need time to think about it.

156
00:08:57,915 --> 00:09:00,304
你有12小时      是吗?
You have 12 hours. Have I?

157
00:09:00,475 --> 00:09:03,672
这只是你虚构的      您是今时的首相
You're inventing this. You are Prime Minister today.

158
00:09:03,835 --> 00:09:06,554
北约总部随时会来电话
The phone might ring now from NATO HQ.

159
00:09:10,835 --> 00:09:13,554
喂? 北约总部 首相
Hello...? Yes. NATO HQ, Prime Minister.

160
00:09:16,675 --> 00:09:19,667
您能参加四月的年会吗?
Can you address their annual conference in April?

161
00:09:19,835 --> 00:09:22,349
我以为可以的 现在我不大确定了
I thought I could. I'm not so sure now.

162
00:09:22,515 --> 00:09:24,267
是
Yes.

163
00:09:24,475 --> 00:09:26,466
第二步
Scenario two.

164
00:09:26,635 --> 00:09:31,151
俄国军队故意跨越了西德的国界
The Russian army cross the West German frontier.

165
00:09:31,315 --> 00:09:33,704
这是最后关头吗?      不是
Is that the last resort? No.

166
00:09:33,875 --> 00:09:36,025
好吧 第三步
Right, scenario three.

167
00:09:36,195 --> 00:09:41,508
假设俄国侵占了西德 比利时 荷兰 法国?
Suppose they invaded West Germany, Belgium, Holland, France?

168
00:09:41,675 --> 00:09:46,669
坦克到了英吉利海峡 整装待发了呢?
their troops have reached the Channel and are poised to invade?

169
00:09:46,835 --> 00:09:49,030
最后关头?      不
Is that the last resort? No.

170
00:09:49,195 --> 00:09:50,708
为什么?
Why not?

171
00:09:50,875 --> 00:09:53,061
我们参与核战的原因是保护自己
We'd only fight a nuclear war to defend ourselves.

172
00:09:53,061 --> 00:09:55,409
怎能用自杀保护自己?
That would be committing suicide!

173
00:09:55,409 --> 00:09:58,353
那什么才是最后关头 皮卡迪利(伦敦商业街)?
So what is the last resort? Piccadilly?

174
00:09:59,395 --> 00:10:01,909
沃特福峡谷维修站?
Watford Gap service station?

175
00:10:02,075 --> 00:10:04,145
革命剧院?
The Reform Club?

176
00:10:04,355 --> 00:10:07,825
也许核武防御根本没意义       它有
Maybe the nuclear deterrent makes no sense. Yes, it does.

177
00:10:07,995 --> 00:10:11,988
如果俄国或者美国有核弹 另一边必须也有
If the Russians or Americans have the bomb, so must the other

178
00:10:12,155 --> 00:10:15,192
留着北极星 以防万一      你的建议呢?
And keep Polaris just in case. What are you proposing?

179
00:10:15,395 --> 00:10:20,913
取消三叉戟订单 省下五十五亿 花在陆军上
Spend the ?5 billion you save on conventional forces.

180
00:10:21,075 --> 00:10:23,801
反正你又不会按那个按钮
You wouldn't really press the button.

181
00:10:23,801 --> 00:10:25,613
如果别无选择 我会的
I might if I had no choice.

182
00:10:25,648 --> 00:10:30,713
不会把你逼到别无选择 他们会用香肠战术
They'll never put you in a situation where you have no choice.

183
00:10:30,915 --> 00:10:35,909
假设我们取消三叉戟 把55亿花在陆军上
Supposing we cancel Trident and support conventional forces?

184
00:10:36,075 --> 00:10:39,909
我们要买什么 坦克?      不 要买ET
What do we spend it on? Tanks? No, we spend it on E.T.

185
00:10:43,155 --> 00:10:45,589
外星人?
Extra-terrestrials?

186
00:10:45,795 --> 00:10:47,911
紧急应对技术
Emergent technology.

187
00:10:50,555 --> 00:10:52,860
那是什么?      智能弹头
What's that? Smart missiles

188
00:10:52,860 --> 00:10:54,712
瞄准系统 红外线
target finding, infrared.

189
00:10:54,747 --> 00:10:58,434
谁来操纵ET呢?      一支庞大的陆军军队
Who would operate this E.T? A large conventional army.

190
00:10:58,635 --> 00:11:00,626
一支庞大的陆……
A large convention...

191
00:11:00,795 --> 00:11:02,865
我有个主意
I've got an idea.

192
00:11:03,595 --> 00:11:05,586
等等
Wait a minute!

193
00:11:05,755 --> 00:11:09,509
我觉得这个计划很可行 第一 取消三叉戟
I think I can see how to do this. First, we cancel Trident.

194
00:11:09,675 --> 00:11:12,189
对      也不再买巡航导弹了
Yes. We don't buy Cruise either.

195
00:11:12,355 --> 00:11:15,347
对      然后恢复征兵制
Yes. Then we introduce conscription.

196
00:11:15,515 --> 00:11:16,834
对
Yes.

197
00:11:16,995 --> 00:11:21,864
不仅解决了国防 还能解决就业问题
Not only solve defence problems but unemployment as well.

198
00:11:22,075 --> 00:11:24,589
首相 征兵会不会太有魄力?
Isn't conscription a courageous policy?

199
00:11:24,795 --> 00:11:27,263
魄力? 老天 会吗?
Courageous? Oh, my God, is it?

200
00:11:28,635 --> 00:11:31,672
不会不会 全额就业率的时候才会
No, no. In times of full employment, it would be.

201
00:11:31,875 --> 00:11:33,178
可现在我们只是
But now we'd just give

202
00:11:33,178 --> 00:11:35,073
给失业的年轻人找点事干
unemployed young people something to do.

203
00:11:35,835 --> 00:11:39,828
教他们各种技巧 甚至可能教会他们认字
teach them trades and skills. even teach them to read.

204
00:11:39,995 --> 00:11:44,466
文盲不能退伍 还能教他们讲点卫生
The army never discharged anyone who was illiterate.

205
00:11:44,635 --> 00:11:49,629
给年轻人全面教育 去弥补他们的素质教育
comprehensive education make up for comprehensive education

206
00:11:51,875 --> 00:11:56,869
就叫它"国民服务"把年轻人都送去社会服务
Call it national service. Send them into the community services

207
00:11:57,035 --> 00:11:59,240
同一个政策 可以解决
With one policy, we solve our

208
00:11:59,240 --> 00:12:02,452
国防 教育 就业问题 对吧教授?
defence, educational and unemployment problems.

209
00:12:02,755 --> 00:12:05,553
这真美妙 我可以预见
This is wonderful. I see it all now.

210
00:12:05,715 --> 00:12:09,503
"大不列颠的新未来 哈克的宏伟蓝图"
''A new deal for Britain Hacker's Grand Design.''

211
00:12:10,435 --> 00:12:13,427
有时 在我们伟大岛国
From time to time in our great island story,

212
00:12:13,595 --> 00:12:16,029
责任会降临于一人...
it falls to one man...

213
00:12:16,635 --> 00:12:19,627
领导人民走出阴影渊谷
to lead his people out of the valley of the shadow

214
00:12:19,795 --> 00:12:23,151
走向和平与繁荣之阳光高原
and into the sunlit uplands of peace and prosperity.

215
00:12:25,515 --> 00:12:27,906
为什么我以前就没想到呢?
Why didn't I think of this before?

216
00:12:27,906 --> 00:12:29,937
因为我们刚见面啊
Because we only just met.

217
00:12:32,675 --> 00:12:34,666
你好 亲爱的
Hello, darling!

218
00:12:35,275 --> 00:12:37,743
午餐吃什么?      你说呢
What's for lunch? You tell me.

219
00:12:40,595 --> 00:12:44,588
你要出去吗?      社工大会 我告诉过你了
Are you going somewhere? Voluntary services committee.

220
00:12:44,755 --> 00:12:49,545
噢 对 我想吃点炒蛋什么的
of course. I just thought a few scrambled eggs or something.

221
00:12:49,715 --> 00:12:52,183
我记得冰箱里还有些鸡蛋
I think there's some eggs in the fridge.

222
00:12:52,355 --> 00:12:56,507
我自己炒?      我们说好的 我继续工作
You want me to do it? We agreed that I'd carry on with my work.

223
00:12:56,675 --> 00:13:00,190
当然      外交部电报 首相
Yes, of course. Foreign Office telegrams, Prime Minister.

224
00:13:00,355 --> 00:13:02,649
放一边吧      再说
Put them over there. It's bad enough

225
00:13:02,649 --> 00:13:04,154
住这个金鱼缸里已经够烦了
living in this goldfish bowl.

226
00:13:04,315 --> 00:13:09,389
每次我出门 都要挤过一打记者 50个游客
I have to walk past a dozen journalists and 50 tourists!

227
00:13:09,555 --> 00:13:12,547
一点隐私都没有      没这回事
There's no privacy anywhere. That's not true.

228
00:13:12,715 --> 00:13:16,833
抱歉 阁下 安全检查 我能四处看看吗?
Sorry, Prime Minister. Security check. Can I just look around?

229
00:13:16,995 --> 00:13:19,350
可以 请吧      隐私?
Yes, carry on. Privacy?

230
00:13:19,515 --> 00:13:21,123
你可以去花园散步嘛
You can always walk in the garden.

231
00:13:21,123 --> 00:13:24,035
被60个人从窗户里盯着看?
With about 60 people staring at you!

232
00:13:24,070 --> 00:13:27,288
像在监狱里放风一样 我们还得
It's like exercising in a prison yard. And we

233
00:13:27,288 --> 00:13:29,534
给这鬼地方付房租 他们应该付我们钱
pay rent for this place. They should pay US!

234
00:13:29,569 --> 00:13:32,267
至少挺安静的
At least it's quiet.

235
00:13:32,435 --> 00:13:35,950
平常很安静的      今早七点半就开始吵了
Usually. That's been going on since half past seven!

236
00:13:36,155 --> 00:13:39,147
他们总得练习吧?      为什么非要在这里?
They've got to practise somewhere. Why here?

237
00:13:39,315 --> 00:13:41,801
他们是皇家骑警啊
That's the Horse Guards' Parade.

238
00:13:41,801 --> 00:13:44,001
检查完毕 阁下 打扰了
All clear, Prime Minister.

239
00:13:44,155 --> 00:13:48,910
安妮 你得明白 人民公仆需要牺牲很多东西的
Annie, a career in public service involves some sacrifice.

240
00:13:49,115 --> 00:13:51,788
好啊 你牺牲你的午餐吧 我快迟到了
Fine, you sacrifice your lunch. I'm late.

241
00:13:52,395 --> 00:13:54,784
可我饿了      噢
I'm hungry! Aw!

242
00:13:55,675 --> 00:13:58,872
你中午吃了什么?      半块巧克力
What did you have for YOUR lunch? Half a Yorkie bar.

243
00:14:00,435 --> 00:14:02,585
另外那半块呢?
Where's the other half?

244
00:14:05,955 --> 00:14:07,946
啊 伯纳
Ah, Bernard!

245
00:14:08,155 --> 00:14:11,147
首相      午餐吃得好吗?
Yes, Prime Minister. Had a good lunch?

246
00:14:11,315 --> 00:14:13,875
还不错 谢谢 首相      在哪吃的?
Oh, quite good. Where did you have it?

247
00:14:14,075 --> 00:14:16,464
内阁餐厅      三道菜?
In the Cabinet mess. Three courses?

248
00:14:16,675 --> 00:14:18,472
是的
Er, yes.

249
00:14:18,635 --> 00:14:21,388
喝了酒?      一杯红酒 是的
Wine? A glass of claret, yes.

250
00:14:22,155 --> 00:14:25,147
想知道我午餐吃了什么吗?
Would you like to know what I had for my lunch?

251
00:14:25,355 --> 00:14:28,904
您想告诉我吗 首相?      什么都没吃
Do you want to tell me, Prime Minister? Nothing!

252
00:14:29,115 --> 00:14:31,106
您在节食?
Are you dieting?

253
00:14:31,995 --> 00:14:36,307
好像这里可以给你和其他秘书提供膳食
It seems there are facilities for feeding allsecretaries,

254
00:14:36,475 --> 00:14:40,374
整个内阁 新闻部 打字小姐 信差
the Cabinet Office, the Press Office, the messengers

255
00:14:40,374 --> 00:14:41,646
就是没有我的 我还住在这里
but not for me and I live here!

256
00:14:41,646 --> 00:14:44,632
抱歉 您太太不能做饭吗?      她要工作
Can't Mrs Hacker cook for you? She's out at work.

257
00:14:44,795 --> 00:14:47,468
我们可以帮您找个厨子      谁付钱?
We'll get you a cook. Who'll pay for it?

258
00:14:47,635 --> 00:14:49,910
您 是您的厨子      多少?
You will. How much?

259
00:14:50,075 --> 00:14:52,794
年薪八千到一万镑      太贵了 我付不起
8,000 to 10,000 a year. I can't afford that!

260
00:14:52,995 --> 00:14:56,112
您可以跟内阁秘书沟通一下      叫他来
Talk to the Cabinet Secretary. Bring him here now.

261
00:14:56,275 --> 00:15:00,268
他就快来了 现在能不能讨论国家大事了?
Shall we press on with the affairs of the nation?

262
00:15:00,475 --> 00:15:03,785
去他的国家大事 我想要个厨子
Stuff the affairs of the nation. I want a cook!

263
00:15:03,995 --> 00:15:06,087
我会帮您找的 同时
I'll look into it.

264
00:15:06,087 --> 00:15:08,169
新闻部的马尔康华伦想跟您谈谈
Malcolm Warren from the Press Office would like a word.

265
00:15:08,169 --> 00:15:10,146
好吧 让他进来
OK, bring him in.

266
00:15:11,995 --> 00:15:15,510
下午好 首相      下午好 马尔康
Good afternoon, Prime Minister. Good afternoon, Malcolm.

267
00:15:15,675 --> 00:15:18,109
内阁秘书要来了 你能说得简洁点吗?
Could we keep this brief?

268
00:15:18,275 --> 00:15:20,273
好的 两件事 第一件最重要
Yes, two things. First, we'll discuss

269
00:15:20,273 --> 00:15:23,080
您的首次首相电视演讲
your first appearance on TV as Prime Minister.

270
00:15:23,080 --> 00:15:25,873
确实重要 得等时间充足的时候
Perhaps we ought to leave it until we've time

271
00:15:25,873 --> 00:15:28,060
深入讨论 第二呢?
to do it thoroughly. What's the other thing?

272
00:15:28,060 --> 00:15:30,832
您对华盛顿的正式访问 次要的      如何?
Your official visit to Washington. What about it?

273
00:15:31,035 --> 00:15:33,708
很多媒体想跟去      让他们跟去
A lot of press want to come. Let them.

274
00:15:33,875 --> 00:15:36,389
很昂贵的      马尔康
It'll be very expensive. Malcolm!

275
00:15:36,555 --> 00:15:41,709
我会在白宫门前 和美国总统肩靠肩地站在一起
I stand on the White House lawn with the President of the USA.

276
00:15:42,595 --> 00:15:45,871
国歌奏响 两位大国领导人站在一起
National anthems, two world leaders together.

277
00:15:46,795 --> 00:15:50,424
显示我们两国之间深厚的友谊与感情
We will tell the world about our happy relationship,

278
00:15:50,595 --> 00:15:52,586
我们的团结 决心
our unity, resolve,

279
00:15:52,755 --> 00:15:56,748
也许聊几句关于我的勇气 智慧 政治才能
a few words perhaps about my own courage, statesmanship.

280
00:15:56,915 --> 00:15:59,998
你难道不明白这对我有多重要
Can't you realise how important this is to me?

281
00:15:59,998 --> 00:16:01,778
不是对我 是对英国
Well, not to me, to Britain.

282
00:16:02,515 --> 00:16:05,791
我们在世界上的地位 我在历史上的地位
Our place in the world, my place in the history books.

283
00:16:05,995 --> 00:16:09,749
是 首相      进来坐 汉弗莱 谢谢 马尔康
Yes, Prime Minister. Come in, Humphrey. Thank you, Malcolm.

284
00:16:10,995 --> 00:16:13,270
马尔康      汉弗莱
Malcolm... Humphrey!

285
00:16:13,955 --> 00:16:16,230
我在思考      很好
I've been thinking... Good.

286
00:16:19,355 --> 00:16:23,064
我做首相有...让我想想 三天了
I've been Prime Minister for, let me see, three days now.

287
00:16:23,275 --> 00:16:26,187
而且是一位很好的首相
And a very good PM you are, too!

288
00:16:26,395 --> 00:16:29,944
我不是让你拍我马屁 虽然确实很顺利
I'm not fishing for compliments, though it has been going well.

289
00:16:30,115 --> 00:16:32,231
哦 当然
Oh, indeed.

290
00:16:32,435 --> 00:16:35,566
能报答老朋友真愉快
It's nice to be able to reward one's old allies.

291
00:16:35,566 --> 00:16:37,893
罗恩琼斯对他的授勋满意吗?
Was Ron Jones pleased with his peerage?

292
00:16:37,893 --> 00:16:40,905
是的 首相 他说他的会员会很高兴
Yes, Prime Minister. He said his members would be delighted.

293
00:16:41,075 --> 00:16:44,704
会员?      工会会员 国家联合...
His members? Of his union. The National Federation...

294
00:16:44,915 --> 00:16:48,146
不是他 我说的是我们的后座议员
I didn't mean him. I meant our backbencher!

295
00:16:48,755 --> 00:16:51,952
我说给罗恩琼斯授勋 不是那个罗恩琼斯
I meant to give a peerage to Ron Jones, not Ron Jones!

296
00:16:54,435 --> 00:16:56,187
真活见鬼了
Bloody hell!

297
00:16:56,395 --> 00:16:59,273
如果这能安慰您的话 我想他非常高兴
If it's any consolation, he was awfully pleased.

298
00:16:59,475 --> 00:17:04,265
他当然了 罗恩琼斯怎么办 也给他授个勋?
I bet he was! What are we going to do about Ron Jones's peerage?

299
00:17:04,475 --> 00:17:07,118
恕我直言 首相 我们不能一下
Prime Minister, we can't send

300
00:17:07,118 --> 00:17:08,981
往上议院塞两个罗恩琼斯爵士
two Lord Ron Jones to the upper house.

301
00:17:09,035 --> 00:17:11,265
看起来像搞批发的
It'll look like a job lot.

302
00:17:12,355 --> 00:17:16,428
我们得给他点什么      他喜欢什么 看电视?
I've got to give him something. Does he watch television?

303
00:17:16,635 --> 00:17:20,753
他根本没电视       好极了 给他BBC吧
He hasn't even got a set. Fine. Make him a governor of the BBC.

304
00:17:21,955 --> 00:17:24,469
还有什么?      还有件小事
Anything else? Yes, one small thing.

305
00:17:24,635 --> 00:17:27,274
我需要一个厨子兼管家
I need a cook/housekeeper for the flat.

306
00:17:27,274 --> 00:17:28,600
您可以登广告
You can advertise.

307
00:17:28,600 --> 00:17:32,383
不 公派的厨子兼管家       这有点困难
No, a government cook/housekeeper. That could be difficult.

308
00:17:32,595 --> 00:17:34,272
为什么?       这是您的私宅
Why? It's a private home.

309
00:17:34,272 --> 00:17:35,723
只不过碰巧是政府办公处
Happen to be in a goverment building

310
00:17:35,723 --> 00:17:37,146
我得住在这 在这吃饭
I happen to be live and eat here

311
00:17:37,146 --> 00:17:39,563
我只想找个人做饭 不是没道理
I just want somebody to cook my lunch. It's not unreasonable.

312
00:17:39,563 --> 00:17:41,391
不 只是不可能
No, it's just not possible.

313
00:17:41,555 --> 00:17:44,786
我有权炸掉全世界 却不能要一盘炒蛋?
I can blow up the world, but not ask for scrambled eggs?

314
00:17:44,995 --> 00:17:49,227
您有权力申请      如果我请德国大使吃饭呢?
You can ASK for them. What if I asked the German ambassador?

315
00:17:49,435 --> 00:17:52,427
这是可以的正式预约 官方招待
That's OK official engagement, government hospitality.

316
00:17:52,595 --> 00:17:54,563
我们很高兴提供七道菜的大餐
We'll provide a seven-course meal

317
00:17:54,563 --> 00:17:55,791
葡萄酒和白兰地 没问题
with wine and brandy.

318
00:17:55,835 --> 00:17:59,623
德国大使的午餐就是政府活动 我的就不是?
The Germans lunch is government business, but mine isn't?

319
00:17:59,795 --> 00:18:01,865
不止德国 对任何大使都是
That is so. Any ambassador's.

320
00:18:02,075 --> 00:18:04,918
好 伯纳 拿我的行程表
Fine. Bernard, get the diary

321
00:18:04,918 --> 00:18:06,996
星期一请德国大使吃午餐
On Monday, I'll have lunch with the German ambassador.

322
00:18:07,235 --> 00:18:11,099
星期二 法国大使 星期三 美国大使
On Tuesday, with the French; Wednesday, with the American

323
00:18:11,099 --> 00:18:15,359
别忘了英联邦 星期四 新西兰专员
on Thursday, with the New Zealand High Commissioner.

324
00:18:15,955 --> 00:18:18,594
联合国有多少个国家?      158
How many countries in the UN? 158.

325
00:18:18,755 --> 00:18:22,191
这能吃六个月了 然后就从头再吃一轮
That'll take up six months, then we'll start round again.

326
00:18:22,355 --> 00:18:25,660
您不能每天都跟大使吃午饭的
You can't have lunch with ambassadors every day

327
00:18:25,660 --> 00:18:27,248
有时候有别的公务宴会
There will be other official lunches.

328
00:18:27,283 --> 00:18:29,703
那更好 可以填补空缺
Even better. We'll fill up the odd gaps.

329
00:18:29,875 --> 00:18:34,232
外交部也许不会同意      怎么
The Foreign Office might have some views on that.

330
00:18:34,395 --> 00:18:37,592
他们说首相跟大使吃一次午餐
They say that one Prime Minister's lunch with an ambassador

331
00:18:37,755 --> 00:18:40,223
破坏两年的外交成果
destroys two years of patient diplomacy.

332
00:18:40,395 --> 00:18:43,273
我不确定他们怎么看待158次午餐
I'm not quite sure how they'd react to 158.

333
00:18:44,035 --> 00:18:46,623
太荒唐了 难道没人给我做饭吗?
It's absurd that no one caters for us here.

334
00:18:46,623 --> 00:18:48,458
这规矩流传250年了
It's been like that for 250 years.

335
00:18:48,493 --> 00:18:51,307
这是最终定论吗?      250年以来 是的
That's the clinching argument? For 250 years, yes.

336
00:18:51,515 --> 00:18:54,712
抱歉 汉弗莱爵士 没有250年来的定论
It can't have been the clinching argument for 250 years.

337
00:18:54,875 --> 00:18:59,073
因为50年前 只能说200年以来
50 years ago, it had been the clinching argument for 200 years

338
00:18:59,275 --> 00:19:01,505
100年前...
and 100 years ago...

339
00:19:02,195 --> 00:19:03,753
抱歉
Sorry.

340
00:19:03,955 --> 00:19:07,451
汉弗莱 我不信这邪 我要一个厨子兼管家
Humphrey, I want a cook/housekeeper

341
00:19:07,451 --> 00:19:08,999
而且我要你找人给她付薪水
and I want you to see that she's paid for.

342
00:19:08,999 --> 00:19:10,984
好吧 让我换个方式说
Well, let me put it like this.

343
00:19:11,155 --> 00:19:15,546
您想要媒体宣布 您当首相以来第一个举措
Do you want the press to announce that your first act

344
00:19:15,715 --> 00:19:19,344
就是给您自己每年加薪1万磅?
was to give yourself a salary increase of ?,000 to ?0,000?

345
00:19:19,515 --> 00:19:21,631
不告诉他们就成了
We wouldn't tell them.

346
00:19:21,795 --> 00:19:25,788
我们别无选择 首相的收支必须要公开
Prime Ministers' expenses must be published.

347
00:19:25,995 --> 00:19:30,830
难道不能隐瞒?      透明政府 信息自由
There's no way that we can't not tell them? Open government.

348
00:19:31,035 --> 00:19:34,823
我们必须开诚布公地告诉媒体
We should always tell the press freely and frankly anything

349
00:19:34,995 --> 00:19:38,351
一切他们自有办法查到的事
that they could easily find out some other way.

350
00:19:38,835 --> 00:19:42,987
一定有办法      250年以来都没有
There must be some solution. There hasn't been for 250 years.

351
00:19:43,155 --> 00:19:48,024
现在能讨论国家大事了吗? 您刚才说您在考虑
Now may we discuss government business?

352
00:19:49,035 --> 00:19:53,426
啊 是的 刚说到我的领导是非常成功的
We're agreed that my premiership has been a great success.

353
00:19:53,635 --> 00:19:55,353
哦 当然
Oh, indeed.

354
00:19:55,515 --> 00:19:59,827
对 我在考虑如何让成功延续下去
what can I do to continue this run of success?

355
00:20:00,035 --> 00:20:03,471
您考虑过"无为"吗?
Have you considered masterly inactivity?

356
00:20:03,675 --> 00:20:06,428
不 汉弗莱 首相必须强硬
No, Humphrey, a Prime Minister must be firm.

357
00:20:07,115 --> 00:20:10,903
当然 那么强硬的无为呢?
Indeed. How about firm masterly inactivity?

358
00:20:11,115 --> 00:20:13,106
不 我要强硬
No, I shall be firm.

359
00:20:13,275 --> 00:20:18,269
我决定取消三叉戟订单 把55亿花到陆军上去
I'll cancel Trident, channel ?5 billion into conventional forces

360
00:20:18,435 --> 00:20:21,074
而且扩大征兵
and reintroduce conscription.

361
00:20:21,235 --> 00:20:25,831
同一个政策 我们可以解决国防 财政平衡
At one stroke, we shall solve our defence, balance of payments,

362
00:20:25,995 --> 00:20:29,510
就业率 教育问题
unemployment and educational problems all at once.

363
00:20:30,355 --> 00:20:32,994
你觉得呢 汉弗莱?
What do you say, Humphrey?

364
00:20:34,755 --> 00:20:39,033
您不能把整个国防部署彻底洗牌啊
You can't reorganise the entire defence of the realm just like that.

365
00:20:39,235 --> 00:20:42,068
我是首相 我有这个权力
I'm the Prime Minister. I have the power.

366
00:20:42,235 --> 00:20:47,229
对 遵循法律和宪法 行政管理的前例
Yes, within the law and the constitution and the precedent,

367
00:20:47,395 --> 00:20:50,193
可行性预算和内阁政府
budgetary feasibility and cabinet government.

368
00:20:50,355 --> 00:20:53,870
您要改买巡航导弹?      不 不再买核武器了
You'll buy Cruise instead? No, no more nuclear weapons.

369
00:20:54,075 --> 00:20:57,306
可首相....您不是秘密的片面限武派吧?
But, Prime Minister... You're not a secret unilateralist?

370
00:20:57,515 --> 00:20:58,673
不是 我们还有北极星呢
No, we still have Polaris.

371
00:20:58,673 --> 00:21:01,503
北极星都老掉牙了
Polaris is a ramshackle old system.

372
00:21:01,675 --> 00:21:07,784
苏联很容易发明个飞弹拦截北极星
The Soviets might develop a ballistic missile defence system

373
00:21:07,995 --> 00:21:11,783
什么时候?      战略角度来说 任何时候
By when? In strategic terms, any day now.

374
00:21:11,955 --> 00:21:14,105
精确一点说 几几年?
By what year precisely?

375
00:21:14,275 --> 00:21:17,347
2020? 但这比你想象要快
2020? But that's sooner than you think!

376
00:21:17,555 --> 00:21:22,549
你是说核武防御能拦截192个北极星吗?
Are you saying that this system would stop all Polaris missiles?

377
00:21:22,715 --> 00:21:25,070
也不是全部 事实上 97%
Not all, virtually all 97%.

378
00:21:25,235 --> 00:21:28,227
有5个炸弹会通过咯?
That would leave five bombs that would get through?

379
00:21:28,435 --> 00:21:29,826
只是5个而已
A mere five!

380
00:21:29,826 --> 00:21:32,752
分别去莫斯科 列宁格勒和明斯克
Obliterating Moscow, Leningrad and Minsk.

381
00:21:32,752 --> 00:21:35,028
是的 但这就是全部了
Yes, but that's about all.

382
00:21:35,195 --> 00:21:37,755
够吓唬俄国人了
Enough to make the Russians stop and think.

383
00:21:37,955 --> 00:21:40,855
但这不公平 有了三叉戟
But it's not fair. With Trident

384
00:21:40,855 --> 00:21:43,061
我们可以扫除整个东欧
we could obliterate the whole of eastern Europe

385
00:21:43,061 --> 00:21:45,282
可我不想扫除东欧      这是个威慑
I don't want to! It's a deterrent.

386
00:21:45,282 --> 00:21:47,083
这是唬人 我大概根本不会用
It's a bluff. I probably wouldn't use it.

387
00:21:47,083 --> 00:21:48,887
可他们不知道您大概不用
They don't know you probably wouldn't.

388
00:21:48,887 --> 00:21:50,161
他们大概知道      对 大概
They probably do. Yes, probably,

389
00:21:50,161 --> 00:21:52,245
但他们不能肯定您真的不用
but they can't certainly know.

390
00:21:52,245 --> 00:21:54,153
他们大概真的知道
They probably certainly know.

391
00:21:54,355 --> 00:21:57,870
对 就算他们可能真的知道您不用
though they probably certainly know that you probably wouldn't,

392
00:21:58,035 --> 00:22:00,549
也不确定 尽管您可能不用
they don't certainly know that although you probably wouldn't,

393
00:22:00,715 --> 00:22:03,229
您就肯定没有可能用
there's no probability that you certainly would!

394
00:22:07,315 --> 00:22:08,794
啥?
What?

395
00:22:09,555 --> 00:22:12,115
归根结底 这是个简单的问题
It all boils down to one simple issue.

396
00:22:12,275 --> 00:22:17,269
您是首相 您不认为英国该拥有最好的吗?
You are the PM. Shouldn't Great Britain have the best?

397
00:22:17,475 --> 00:22:19,352
那当然了      很好
Yes, of course.

398
00:22:19,515 --> 00:22:23,906
如果您走进核武展览会 您就会买三叉戟
If you walked into a showroom, you would buy Trident!

399
00:22:24,075 --> 00:22:26,794
它那么可爱 优雅 美丽
It's lovely, it's elegant, it's beautiful.

400
00:22:26,955 --> 00:22:30,948
它显然是最好的 而英国应该拥有最好的
It is quite simply the best, and Britain should have the best.

401
00:22:31,115 --> 00:22:34,869
在核武世界中 它是萨维罗西装
In the world of the nuclear missile, it is the Savile Row suit,

402
00:22:35,035 --> 00:22:37,310
劳斯莱斯轿车
the Rolls-Royce Corniche,

403
00:22:37,475 --> 00:22:39,989
1945年的拉菲红酒
the Ch鈚eau Lafite 1945.

404
00:22:40,155 --> 00:22:44,068
是哈罗德(伦敦豪华商场)会卖的导弹
It is the nuclear missile Harrods would sell you.

405
00:22:46,915 --> 00:22:49,349
我还用多说吗?
What more can I say?

406
00:22:49,515 --> 00:22:52,075
除了它要花55亿 我们根本用不上
That it costs ?5 billion and we don't need it.

407
00:22:52,235 --> 00:22:54,749
哈罗德卖的东西不都这样
You can say that about anything at Harrods.

408
00:23:06,635 --> 00:23:09,627
将军 我正想和您谈谈
Ah, General! I was hoping to have a word with you.

409
00:23:09,795 --> 00:23:13,470
我想问您些事情 您不一定爱听
I wanted to sound you out about something. You'll not like it.

410
00:23:13,635 --> 00:23:15,163
尽管说 首相
Tell me the worst.

411
00:23:15,163 --> 00:23:18,517
军方可能不大欢迎 那也没辙
It will be very unpopular with the services.

412
00:23:18,517 --> 00:23:20,669
我计划取消三叉戟      好主意
I'm planning to cancel Trident. Good idea.

413
00:23:20,835 --> 00:23:24,623
别忙 别太快下结论 先别争论...
don't jump in too quickly. No good trying to argue...

414
00:23:25,315 --> 00:23:27,783
你刚才说什么?      好主意
What did you say? It's a good idea.

415
00:23:27,955 --> 00:23:30,047
你同意 为什么?      当然
You're in favour? Why?

416
00:23:30,047 --> 00:23:32,715
我们根本不需要 完全是浪费钱
We don't need it. Complete waste of money.

417
00:23:32,715 --> 00:23:34,163
和我说的一样      您说得对
That's what I said. You're right.

418
00:23:34,955 --> 00:23:38,743
国防部都同意吗?      海军想保留
The whole defence staff agree? The navy want to keep it.

419
00:23:38,915 --> 00:23:40,363
要放在他们潜艇上
On their ships.

420
00:23:40,363 --> 00:23:42,806
拿走三叉戟 他们就没什么重要性了
Take away Trident and they'd hardly have a role left.

421
00:23:42,915 --> 00:23:45,429
空军呢?       您可以问他们
And the RAF? You could ask them.

422
00:23:45,595 --> 00:23:46,974
如果您想知道车间机械师的想法
If you're interested in the opinion of garage mechanics

423
00:23:48,051 --> 00:23:49,513
他们希望保留
They'd want to keep it.

424
00:23:50,235 --> 00:23:52,749
他们想驾驶飞机从空中丢炸弹
They want to drop the bomb from an aeroplane.

425
00:23:52,915 --> 00:23:56,703
他们就喜欢从空中往下丢东西 但又丢不准
They just like dropping things on people, no good at it.

426
00:23:56,915 --> 00:23:59,429
甚至无法接近史丹利港口跑道
Couldn't even close the runway at Port Stanley.

427
00:23:59,595 --> 00:24:00,861
也许永远找不到莫斯科
Probably never find Moscow,

428
00:24:00,861 --> 00:24:03,225
就算找到了 也打不中
and if they did they'd miss it.

429
00:24:03,225 --> 00:24:07,068
如果军方喜欢 怎么才能让这政策通过呢?
How do we get the policy through if only the army is in favour?

430
00:24:07,235 --> 00:24:10,910
您知道 国防部人事处长职位快出缺了
As you know, the Chief of Defence Staff job is becoming vacant.

431
00:24:11,075 --> 00:24:14,192
理论上该轮到海军了 但这是您的决定
Technically, it's the navy's turn, but it's your decision.

432
00:24:14,355 --> 00:24:16,823
只要您高兴 可以任命任何士兵
If you appoint a soldier, it's up to you.

433
00:24:17,035 --> 00:24:20,186
将军 您不正是最资深的士兵吗?
General, aren't you the most senior soldier?

434
00:24:20,395 --> 00:24:22,784
碰巧 我也这么想
As it happens, I believe I am.

435
00:24:23,395 --> 00:24:25,545
谢谢 很好的建议
Thank you. Good advice.

436
00:24:25,715 --> 00:24:27,831
首相 这是格拉索夫人
Prime Minister, this is Mrs Glossop.

437
00:24:28,795 --> 00:24:30,831
太神奇了      怎么了?
Extraordinary thing! What?

438
00:24:30,995 --> 00:24:33,987
总算发现一位有点理智的首相了
I've come across a Prime Minister with a bit of sense.

439
00:24:34,155 --> 00:24:36,623
是吗 哪里的? 哪个幸运的国家?
Really? Where? Which is the lucky country?

440
00:24:37,795 --> 00:24:40,046
我们的 他想取消三叉戟
Ours. He's cancelling Trident.

441
00:24:40,046 --> 00:24:41,786
我简直不相信我的耳朵
I could hardly believe my ears.

442
00:24:41,786 --> 00:24:44,439
真惊讶你居然会喜欢恢复征兵
I'm surprised you're happy about reintroducing conscription.

443
00:24:45,355 --> 00:24:47,485
征兵? 他没提征兵
He didn't say anything about conscription.

444
00:24:47,485 --> 00:24:50,329
正是如此 降低失业率 捞选票
Slashes unemployment, wins votes.

445
00:24:50,329 --> 00:24:53,158
征兵? 我们是世界级精锐部队
We're an elite army, best in the world.

446
00:24:53,158 --> 00:24:54,765
专业 勇敢 有纪律
Professional, tough, disciplined.

447
00:24:54,765 --> 00:24:57,682
我们可不要一堆小流氓
We can't bring in a mob of punks

448
00:24:57,682 --> 00:24:59,302
怪胎 瘾君子 神经病
and freaks and junkies and riff-raff.

449
00:24:59,835 --> 00:25:02,734
25万足球流氓?
A quarter of a million football hooligans?

450
00:25:03,115 --> 00:25:05,055
在陆军基地削土豆皮?
Peeling potatoes in Aldershot?

451
00:25:05,055 --> 00:25:06,520
就知道你会这么说
I thought you'd say that.

452
00:25:06,795 --> 00:25:08,364
会成为普通军队的
It'll be just an ordinary army.

453
00:25:08,364 --> 00:25:10,544
就像赢了二战那一支?
Like the one that won the last war?

454
00:25:10,875 --> 00:25:13,867
平等机会纯属胡闹 像美国一样
All this equal opportunity nonsense, like America!

455
00:25:14,035 --> 00:25:18,311
士兵到达之前 他们都不知道是男是女
They don't know if the troops posted to them are men or women

456
00:25:18,311 --> 00:25:21,213
有时候到了也不知道      对
Sometimes not even then. Quite!

457
00:25:21,755 --> 00:25:23,628
保留三叉戟要好得多
Much better to keep Trident.

458
00:25:23,628 --> 00:25:25,438
就知道你会这么说
I thought you'd say that.

459
00:25:25,438 --> 00:25:26,397
我们得阻止他 你去阻止他
You must stop him.

460
00:25:26,397 --> 00:25:28,955
没法就这样阻止首相
One can't just stop the Prime Minister.

461
00:25:29,355 --> 00:25:31,497
我们要做什么?      让他降降速
What do we do? We must slow him down.

462
00:25:31,995 --> 00:25:33,756
反正一两个月后
After a few months, most new Prime Ministers

463
00:25:33,756 --> 00:25:35,887
大多数首相动力都会少一半
have more or less ground to a halt anyway.

464
00:25:37,155 --> 00:25:41,148
所以 明早我和美国大使谈谈
I'll have a word with the American ambassador tomorrow morning.

465
00:25:41,315 --> 00:25:43,783
好主意      就知道你会这么说
Good idea. I thought you'd say that.

466
00:25:43,955 --> 00:25:45,468
哦 你好
Oh, hello!

467
00:25:45,635 --> 00:25:47,762
新闻部要保证BBC和ITN
I want to make sure that the BBC and ITN

468
00:25:47,762 --> 00:25:49,614
都在白宫草地上占有利地形
get good coverage on the White House lawn.

469
00:25:49,614 --> 00:25:51,653
拍我和总统的特写      好
Shot of me and the President

470
00:25:52,186 --> 00:25:56,312
还有白宫内部 就我和总统两个人
Then there'll be more photo coverage inside the White House.

471
00:25:56,515 --> 00:25:58,028
很好
Splendid.

472
00:25:58,195 --> 00:25:59,618
还要拍我和总统
Then there'll be coverage of

473
00:25:59,618 --> 00:26:01,766
第二天会谈开始的情形      好
me and the President at the start of talks the next day.

474
00:26:02,782 --> 00:26:05,029
然后是总统对我说再见的时候
Then the President will say goodbye to me.

475
00:26:05,029 --> 00:26:07,445
我希望他能用左手扶着我的手肘
I hope he takes my elbow with his left hand.

476
00:26:07,445 --> 00:26:09,967
就像对德国总理那样      德国总理
He did that with the West German Chancellor.

477
00:26:11,740 --> 00:26:14,617
能不能跟大使馆说说 预定这个动作?
Any chance of ensuring that beforehand with the embassy?

478
00:26:14,617 --> 00:26:18,029
可能很困难 您能看看内阁议程吗?
That could be difficult. Could you look at the Cabinet agenda?

479
00:26:18,235 --> 00:26:20,703
我真不知道我们设立个大使馆作甚
I don't know what we have embassies for.

480
00:26:20,875 --> 00:26:22,402
每次你要求他们做点重要的事
Any time you ask them to do something really important

481
00:26:22,402 --> 00:26:24,038
对英国重要的
important for Britain...

482
00:26:25,555 --> 00:26:28,068
我们不是要讨论取消三叉戟吗?
Weren't we to discuss scrapping Trident?

483
00:26:28,068 --> 00:26:30,300
当然要讨论 首相
Indeed we were, Prime Minister.

484
00:26:30,300 --> 00:26:32,592
但我认为您该首先
But I thought in the first instance you might

485
00:26:32,592 --> 00:26:34,456
周详考虑一下才明智
think it wiser to go into it thoroughly,

486
00:26:34,456 --> 00:26:40,095
讨论各种潜在可能性 这可是帝国的国防
as we are discussing the defence of the realm.

487
00:26:40,095 --> 00:26:41,378
你想阻止我 汉弗莱
You're trying to stop me, Humphrey.

488
00:26:41,378 --> 00:26:45,186
不 首相 但内阁必须周详考虑
No, but the Cabinet must have all the facts.

489
00:26:45,186 --> 00:26:46,786
这倒新鲜
That's a novel idea.

490
00:26:47,395 --> 00:26:50,726
有个特殊理由 我认为您可能想要暂缓
There is a reason why I thought you might leave it for a while.

491
00:26:50,726 --> 00:26:55,347
什么      美国大使私下告诉我
I've learned from the American ambassador informally

492
00:26:55,347 --> 00:26:57,132
他们会非常不悦
that they would be very upset

493
00:26:57,315 --> 00:26:59,236
如果取消三叉戟订单
if we were to cancel Trident

494
00:26:59,236 --> 00:27:01,696
并不再从他们那里购买任何核武
and not order another of their missiles instead.

495
00:27:01,755 --> 00:27:04,474
我可以和总统当面商讨这件麻烦事
I might as well have it out with the President.

496
00:27:04,675 --> 00:27:06,619
问题就在这里 首相
That's the point.

497
00:27:06,619 --> 00:27:10,825
您与总统会面的议程必须事先议定
The agenda of your meeting must be agreed in advance.

498
00:27:10,825 --> 00:27:13,091
您不能飘洋过海 跑那里去东扯西拉
You can't just go over there for a chat.

499
00:27:13,091 --> 00:27:15,310
为什么不?      呃 您...
Why not? Well, you...

500
00:27:15,915 --> 00:27:18,383
您也许会找不到话说
You might not think of anything to say.

501
00:27:19,315 --> 00:27:24,753
如果您非要向美国人提这个 计划会改变
If this proposal were put to them there will be a change of plan.

502
00:27:24,955 --> 00:27:26,624
什么改变?
What change of plan?

503
00:27:26,624 --> 00:27:29,345
您将不会与总统会面
Your meeting would not be with the President.

504
00:27:29,345 --> 00:27:32,903
改由副总统接待      副总统?
You'd be entertained by the Vice-President. The Vice-President?!

505
00:27:33,075 --> 00:27:36,750
副总统? 你开玩笑吧       恐怕是的 首相
You can't be serious! I'm afraid so, Prime Minister.

506
00:27:36,955 --> 00:27:39,889
连博茨瓦纳总理都见到总统了
Even Botswana was met by the President.

507
00:27:39,889 --> 00:27:40,931
我在新闻上看见了
I saw it on the news.

508
00:27:41,075 --> 00:27:44,306
博茨瓦纳没有取消三叉戟订单
Botswana hadn't just cancelled an order for Trident.

509
00:27:44,475 --> 00:27:48,185
他们肯定会解释说 总统得了结膜炎
I'm sure they'll explain that the President had catarrh

510
00:27:48,185 --> 00:27:49,798
或伤了大拇指什么的
or bruised his thumb or something.

511
00:27:50,595 --> 00:27:52,745
或者是睡过头了
Fallen asleep perhaps.

512
00:27:54,355 --> 00:27:56,869
这次会晤是至关重要的公关事件
This meeting with the President is vital for PR.

513
00:27:57,075 --> 00:28:00,226
所以您应该暂缓三叉戟的事
Then you should postpone the Trident discussion.

514
00:28:00,435 --> 00:28:02,648
汉弗莱 首相必须显示 唐宁街10号里
A Prime Minister must show that there is

515
00:28:02,648 --> 00:28:05,896
有新的思维和强硬的双手
a new mind and a firm hand at Number 10.

516
00:28:05,896 --> 00:28:08,223
他必须显得有所作为
He must be seen to have made his mark.

517
00:28:08,395 --> 00:28:10,909
但是您有啊 首相      什么?
But you have, Prime Minister. How?

518
00:28:13,675 --> 00:28:18,191
一个厨子 从内阁餐厅里出?
A cook... seconded from the Cabinet Office canteen?

519
00:28:20,915 --> 00:28:23,713
在这里的公寓给我做午餐?
To cook lunch for me here at the flat?

520
00:28:23,875 --> 00:28:27,788
您所有前任首相都没做到的事
Something that none of your predecessors ever accomplished.

521
00:28:30,555 --> 00:28:35,626
史书中的位置      就说嘛
A place in the history books.I say!

522
00:28:35,626 --> 00:28:37,990
让他们看看谁说话算数 是吗?
We've shown them who's in charge, haven't we?

523
00:28:38,195 --> 00:28:40,663
的确 首相
Indeed we have, Prime Minister.

524
00:28:40,835 --> 00:28:43,713
新思想 强硬的双手和三叉戟
A new mind and a firm hand and Trident.

525
00:28:43,915 --> 00:28:46,383
史书中的位置啊
A place in the history books, you say.

526
00:28:46,555 --> 00:28:50,045
哦 暂时取消三叉戟的内阁议程
Oh, leave Trident off the Cabinet agenda for the time being

527
00:28:50,045 --> 00:28:52,279
这是我强硬的决定 好吗?
That is my firm decision. All right?

528
00:28:52,279 --> 00:28:54,690
是 首相
Yes, Prime Minister.

529
00:28:57,132 --> 00:29:12,812
